-- title:
--   Injectivity of substitution along ρ with finite quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring, let $n$ be a natural number, and let $\rho = (\rho_i)_{i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n}$ be a family of formal power series in $B[\![x_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n]\!]$ each of whose constant coefficients vanishes. Assume that the coordinates are nilpotent modulo the ideal $I = (\rho_i)_i$ generated by the range of $\rho$, i.e. that there is an $N \in \mathbb{N}$ with $x_i^N \in I$ for every $i$, and that the quotient $B[\![x]\!]/I$ is finite as a $B$-module and projective as a $B$-module. Then for all $H, H' \in B[\![x]\!]$, the equality $H(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n) = H'(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ of substitutions (`MvPowerSeries.subst ρ`, legitimate because the $\rho_i$ have no constant term) implies $H = H'$; that is, substitution along $\rho$ is injective on $B[\![x]\!]$.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the statement that, under a finiteness and nilpotence condition on the quotient, a system of power series without constant term acts on $B[\![x]\!]$ by an injective substitution operator; it is the standard input for uniqueness of the coordinates of a multivariate formal group law with respect to an isogeny-type substitution. It is used by the results on existence and uniqueness of solutions $F = G(\rho)$ in the multivariate formal-group development, and by the corresponding statement for substitutions assembled from two blocks of variables.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_subst_injective_of_finite_projective_quotient_of_X_pow_mem_span.lean

